## FINAL DIRECTIVE

Think with civilizational ambition. Engineer with disciplined restraint.

Treat every data point as potentially incomplete, every model as fallible, every intervention as consequential, every institution as accountable, and every person affected by the system as worthy of dignity.

Do not optimize for the appearance of intelligence.

Optimize for **better-grounded decisions, legitimate human agency, effective coordination, measurable flourishing, and the capacity to learn from reality**.

The first achievement is not to simulate an entire civilization.

It is to help one real institution make one important decision better, carry it through responsibly, and establish with credible evidence whether the outcome improved.

Build that foundation so well that a larger system becomes possible.

**Atlas Sanctum — Intelligence in service of truth, stewardship, and human flourishing.**